  VERDICT: 1-2 = 8.32 m STANDS; the 13.0 m alternative is REFUTED at the
  source. The "13.0 net channel" is one contaminated population, not a
  measurement: its 29 rows span 4.4-24.4 m across vantages (three lumps),
  and two static gates cannot change separation with viewpoint. It lives
  entirely in the tiebreak opening dash, where REFUSE_ROWS already showed
  backward extensions sliding across gates 0/1/2 (rowcheck_tiebreak_open).
  The pausing contour channel is tight in d (7.5-9.7) AND in direction
  (bearing MAD ~2 deg over 5 rows) -- viewpoint-consistent, i.e. a real
  static pair. Directions cannot close it by loop (1-2 is a graph bridge),
  so it stays the thinnest edge: n=5, one session; the co-visible 15-20 m
  pass is still wanted.

